WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:05.359
It feels like it's been ages since the second
season of Westworld ended in a dazzling spectacle

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:08.520
of sacrifice, splendor, and of course gunshots.

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:13.170
In a way, the long wait for season 3 feels
appropriate for a show that has always played

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:16.520
fast and loose with its viewers' perception
of the passage of time.

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:21.710
Now that season 3 is almost here, fans of
HBO's mind-bending sci-fi western are hoping

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:26.540
to soon find answers to many of the questions
raised in the shocking season two finale,

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:27.460
"The Passenger."

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:31.780
What can we expect when we return to the show's
mesmerizing, robot-filled universe?

00:00:31.790 --> 00:00:35.860
Watch on as we round up all the information
we could find about what lies in store for

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:37.860
us in season three of Westworld.

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:44.400
After a seemingly interminable 21-month hiatus,
Westworld's third season will finally premiere

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:46.980
on HBO on March 15, 2020.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:51.870
The series announced its return date via a
perplexing tweet in January of 2020, which

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:55.440
was accompanied by a video outlining the timeline
of the "Divergence."

00:00:55.760 --> 00:01:00.750
The Divergence began in 2019 with some events
that have already happened in the real world,

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:05.139
hinting that Westworld's third season may
wind up hitting uncomfortably close to home.

00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:09.300
The video then goes on to catalog points in
the "Divergence" that haven't happened yet,

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:14.300
ending with the most recent "Divergence,"
in 2058, as the voiceover worries that there

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:16.080
may be someone they haven't accounted for.

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:20.920
While it's easy to assume that the 2058 incident
refers to the Host uprising at the end of

00:01:20.929 --> 00:01:26.189
season 2, that event actually takes place
in 2052, according to security footage of

00:01:26.189 --> 00:01:28.140
Maeve's escape at the end of season one.

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:32.680
This raises the question of just what occurs
six years later, and to whom exactly the video

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:33.680
is referring.

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:38.700
While a number of familiar faces are returning
for season three, the end of season two marked

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:40.780
a definitive farewell for several others.

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:45.200
Anthony Hopkins' park creator Robert Ford
has been dead since the end of season one,

00:01:45.209 --> 00:01:49.509
and although he continued to appear regularly
in flashbacks and visions, co-creator Lisa

00:01:49.509 --> 00:01:52.060
Joy confirmed that he's now gone for good.

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:56.859
Meanwhile, Jimmi Simpson's character, William,
will still be very much alive in season three,

00:01:56.859 --> 00:02:01.409
but will be portrayed exclusively by Ed Harris,
as Simpson revealed at TCA that he hasn't

00:02:01.409 --> 00:02:02.380
been asked to return.

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:06.820
As for Shannon Woodward's determined truth-seeker
Elsie, she was tragically murdered at the

00:02:06.829 --> 00:02:11.760
end of season two, and showrunner Jonathan
Nolan has confirmed that for now, at least,

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:12.860
Elsie is truly gone.

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:16.590
Less clear is the fate of James Marsden's
stalwart cowboy, Teddy.

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:20.870
Teddy committed suicide near the end of season
two, determined to die rather than become

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:25.260
a monster but Dolores [ left his brain pearl
in the Forge, leaving his consciousness free

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:26.960
to cross over into the Sublime.

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:32.020
Nothing has yet been said one way or another
about Marsden's return, but since this is

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:34.140
Westworld, we know better than to rule anything
out.

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:38.099
As for the hosts whose consciousnesses crossed
into the grassy plains of the Sublime while

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:40.080
their mechanical bodies plummeted off a cliff?

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:45.540
Showrunner Lisa Joy confirmed they're gone
for good, including Ghost Nation leader Akecheta,

00:02:45.549 --> 00:02:48.110
his lost love Kohana, and Maeve's daughter.

00:02:48.110 --> 00:02:50.280
Speaking to The Hollywood Reporter, Joy said,

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:52.579
"The stakes and the finality of it are important.

00:02:52.579 --> 00:02:56.630
It's not something where I think the humans
can type it up and get back in and start messing

00:02:56.630 --> 00:02:57.360
with them anymore.

00:02:57.620 --> 00:03:01.940
It's what so many hosts sacrificed so much
for, to see their kind to this safe space."

00:03:02.959 --> 00:03:07.159
By the end of season two, the real Charlotte
Hale is dead and gone, murdered by her host

00:03:07.159 --> 00:03:10.390
doppelgänger, which was imbued with the consciousness
of Dolores.

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:14.820
However, this new, host version of Charlotte
successfully makes it out of the park, as

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:19.549
does Bernard, and is ultimately able to construct
a new Dolores host body to inhabit.

00:03:19.549 --> 00:03:23.860
However, when asked by Entertainment Weekly
whether season three will follow double Doloreses,

00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:25.160
Jonathan Nolan responded,

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:26.040
"Not really.

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:29.980
The question of who's who and what we're looking
at is something we're excited to play with.

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:33.499
We're excited to withhold a little from the
audience but ... it's complicated."

00:03:33.499 --> 00:03:37.969
It's an intriguing answer, and one Tessa Thompson
is eager to explore in season three.

00:03:37.969 --> 00:03:41.620
In an interview with The Hollywood Reporter,
Thompson said of her new identity,

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:43.140
"It's a total game changer.

00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:45.349
I want to put on a lot of different characters.

00:03:45.349 --> 00:03:48.360
That to me is the real exciting potential
in all of this."

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:52.680
Thompson has also said that while in the past,
her character has seemed unsympathetic to

00:03:52.689 --> 00:03:56.360
the hosts' experiences and the fact that they're
not in control of their own lives, we may

00:03:56.360 --> 00:03:58.420
see a different side of her in season 3.

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:01.709
"but I think what we come to learn in the
third season is that the world that Hale comes

00:04:01.709 --> 00:04:06.799
from is maybe not so dissimilar, and that's
something that I have found really fascinating

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:07.940
about this season."

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:11.360
Thompson's host wasn't the only one to make
it out of the park in the season two finale,

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:11.860
though.

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:16.320
Before she left, she took five pearl-shaped
control units, each housing the consciousness

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:17.080
of one host.

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:21.420
Just which hosts they are remains to be seen,
and according to Jonathan Nolan, not even

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:25.900
the writers had fully decided who was in Dolores'
purse at the end of season two.

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:30.330
However, when the inhabitants of those pearls
are eventually revealed in season three, Nolan

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:34.260
said that the goal of the writers is for their
choices to "surprise and hopefully delight"

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:34.860
their audience.

00:04:35.260 --> 00:04:38.970
While we can rule out any of the characters
that we saw cross into the Sublime, that still

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:42.660
leaves a large number of hosts to pick from,
so place your bets wisely.

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:47.720
Since the early days of Westworld, fans have
suspected that Ashley Stubbs, the park's chief

00:04:47.730 --> 00:04:52.360
of security, may be a host, a theory that
only continued to gain traction once other

00:04:52.360 --> 00:04:55.980
characters previously presumed to be human
were revealed to be hosts.

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:59.670
This theory was seemingly confirmed in "The
Passenger," during an intriguing exchange

00:04:59.670 --> 00:05:04.090
between Stubbs and the host that looks like
Charlotte Hale, but is being driven by Dolores.

00:05:04.090 --> 00:05:08.820
During their brief conversation, Stubbs obviously
realizes that Hale isn't all that she seems.

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:12.780
But instead of turning her in, he tells her
that he was hired so long ago he can barely

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:17.110
remember it, saying that Ford was always very
clear about his role at the park, and who

00:05:17.110 --> 00:05:18.640
he was supposed to be loyal to.

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:22.200
"Guess you could call it my core drive."

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:26.070
After musing for a bit over how the lines
have since blurred, making it hard for him

00:05:26.070 --> 00:05:30.260
to know where his loyalties should lie, Stubbs
tells her that she's free to go, after making

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:33.100
it very clear that he knows who and what she
is.

00:05:33.260 --> 00:05:34.900
"I'm responsible for every host.

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:39.020
Inside the park."

00:05:39.220 --> 00:05:43.800
We expect to see more of how Stubbs fits into
Ford's plan when he returns in Westworld season

00:05:43.800 --> 00:05:44.300
three.

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:48.840
While the first two seasons of Westworld have
been told mostly from the points of view of

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:53.240
Dolores and William, otherwise known as the
Man in Black, season three seems to be taking

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:54.460
a sharp left turn.

00:05:54.460 --> 00:05:58.420
The first intriguing glimpse at Westworld's
new season followed a brand new character

00:05:58.420 --> 00:06:02.550
named Caleb, played by Aaron Paul, through
a series of events in what appears to be the

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:04.580
"real" world outside of Delos' park.

00:06:04.810 --> 00:06:09.480
Paul cryptically told The Wrap that his character
will bring excitement, danger, suspense and

00:06:09.490 --> 00:06:14.140
honesty to the series, but other than that,
he's playing his cards very close to the vest

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:16.500
when it comes to Caleb, revealing only that,

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:19.920
"He is a construction worker with a good friend,
George, his robot.

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:20.720
He's a red robot."

00:06:20.720 --> 00:06:26.220
According to Jonathan Nolan, Caleb will "challenge
Dolores' notions about the nature of humanity,"

00:06:26.230 --> 00:06:29.770
although whether her interactions with Caleb
will soften her feelings toward humans or

00:06:29.770 --> 00:06:34.520
just further convince her that her ruthless
attitude is justified is yet to be determined.

00:06:34.520 --> 00:06:35.980
All Paul can tell us is,

00:06:35.980 --> 00:06:44.560
"He crosses paths with this lovely, lovely
being very soon and they create a relationship."

00:06:45.560 --> 00:06:49.890
In addition to Breaking Bad star Aaron Paul,
other new additions to the season three cast

00:06:49.890 --> 00:06:55.230
include Master of None's Lena Waithe, former
NFL running back Marshawn Lynch, and rapper

00:06:55.230 --> 00:06:58.170
Kid Cudi, credited on the show as Scott Mescudi.

00:06:58.170 --> 00:07:02.440
No details have been revealed about any of
their characters, but judging by the trailer,

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:06.810
it appears as though Waithe and Lynch will
be playing Paul's accomplices in various illegal

00:07:06.810 --> 00:07:10.760
activities, while Cudi's character will be
spending at least some of his time in prison.

00:07:10.760 --> 00:07:15.060
Additionally, Vincent Cassel will be coming
aboard as season three's new villain, who

00:07:15.060 --> 00:07:19.840
can be seen in the final trailer for Westworld's
third season making Maeve an intriguing offer.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:21.000
"Dolores.

00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:23.800
I want you to track her down and kill her."

00:07:24.520 --> 00:07:29.040
While viewers of Westworld are no strangers
to artificial lifeforms, season 3 will introduce

00:07:29.050 --> 00:07:33.070
us to a different type of robot than the human-presenting
hosts we're used to.

00:07:33.070 --> 00:07:36.980
George is a standard construction robot, Delos
model G-267.

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:41.520
Built to serve as a helpful co-worker for
Caleb, George doesn't speak, and likely won't

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:45.060
have much in common with his mechanical counterparts
from inside the park.

00:07:45.220 --> 00:07:48.500
Speaking about Dolores and the other hosts
who escaped the park into the real world at

00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:50.980
the end of the second season, Jonathan Nolan
said,

00:07:51.160 --> 00:07:54.540
"Part of what our hosts find [is that] they're
caught in between they're fashioned to look

00:07:54.550 --> 00:07:58.690
like human beings and act like them, but they
have more in common with the mechanical pieces

00:07:58.690 --> 00:07:59.260
in our world."

00:07:59.690 --> 00:08:03.340
Robots like George and the other real-world
worker-bots will play an important role in

00:08:03.340 --> 00:08:07.480
the upcoming season, contrasting the human-like
traits of the hosts with their mechanical

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:07.980
origins.

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:11.200
According to Nolan, these more utilitarian
robots have...

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:15.070
"...been designed for a specific purpose,
and the hosts have been designed to be emotional

00:08:15.070 --> 00:08:16.060
mirrors for us.”

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:20.440
Although a few main characters managed to
escape at the end of season two, there are

00:08:20.440 --> 00:08:25.100
still others left on the inside, with several
areas of Ford's bizarre theme parks as yet

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:25.720
unexplored.

00:08:25.780 --> 00:08:30.600
In addition to Westworld, season two introduced
viewers to Shogunworld and The Raj, but the

00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:35.130
show's official Delos Destinations website
teases three additional parks.

00:08:35.130 --> 00:08:38.990
We may very well travel to one or more of
these remaining parks in season three.

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:42.970
Nolan and Joy have previously hinted that
the show may eventually visit the Roman and

00:08:42.970 --> 00:08:47.060
Medieval Worlds from Michael Crichton's original
1973 movie.

00:08:47.200 --> 00:08:51.080
As for the sixth world, it may have already
been revealed in the season 3 trailer, which

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:55.700
shows Maeve in a place that looks a lot like
Nazi-occupied Europe during World War II.

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:59.660
This also seems to match the glitchy image
of the third park on the Delos website, which

00:08:59.660 --> 00:09:03.800
seems to show planes flying over a light brick
town with smoke rising from it.

00:09:03.800 --> 00:09:08.210
While at first glance, World War II doesn't
exactly seem like a prime vacation spot, if

00:09:08.210 --> 00:09:11.890
there's one thing we've learned about the
elite clientele of Delos' theme parks, it's

00:09:11.890 --> 00:09:15.420
that they're drawn to violent settings where
enemies lurk around every corner.

00:09:15.560 --> 00:09:19.640
But since a World War II park is possibly
an even worse place for a woman of color to

00:09:19.640 --> 00:09:23.720
exist than a Wild West park, we can only hope
that Maeve isn't stuck there for long.

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:28.860
In the final moments of the Westworld season
2 finale, we follow Ed Harris' William as

00:09:28.870 --> 00:09:33.450
he stumbles out of an elevator, badly injured,
and meets his daughter Emily in the rubble

00:09:33.450 --> 00:09:35.760
of what he assumes must be part of the park.

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:39.920
Since he actually killed Emily earlier in
the season, William assumes his consciousness

00:09:39.920 --> 00:09:44.080
has been uploaded to the Forge, but she assures
him that what he's experiencing is real.

00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:45.560
"I'm already in the thing, aren't I?"

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:50.680
"No, the System's long gone."

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:54.560
The conversation that follows echoes the ones
that we saw earlier in the season between

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:59.310
the younger William and James Delos, in which
William repeatedly tested the host body that

00:09:59.310 --> 00:10:02.680
housed Delos' consciousness, waiting for it
to break down.

00:10:02.680 --> 00:10:06.810
William discerns that he's now a host, and
when he asks how many times he's been tested,

00:10:06.810 --> 00:10:08.810
Emily responds that it's been "a long time."

00:10:08.810 --> 00:10:12.120
Speaking to The Wrap about William and Emily's
scene, Lisa Joy said,

00:10:12.120 --> 00:10:13.960
"He’s in a very different timeline.

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:17.330
The whole place looks destroyed, and then
she explains that all of that stuff happened

00:10:17.330 --> 00:10:18.100
long ago.

00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:19.040
That was real.

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:22.720
But now something has happened and the Man
is now the subject or some iteration of the

00:10:22.730 --> 00:10:24.860
Man is now the subject of testing.

00:10:24.860 --> 00:10:26.820
The roles have become completely reversed."

00:10:27.300 --> 00:10:31.500
The final trailer for Westworld season 3 looks
very different than anything we've seen from

00:10:31.500 --> 00:10:32.520
the show before.

00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:36.210
While we do seem to get a couple glimpses
of parks, most of it appears to be set in

00:10:36.210 --> 00:10:40.070
the "real" world, where Dolores and Caleb
will join forces with the Host modeled after

00:10:40.070 --> 00:10:43.350
Charlotte Hale, although she worries that
they are severely outnumbered.

00:10:43.350 --> 00:10:48.140
"Five of us against an entire world of them."

00:10:48.940 --> 00:10:49.780
Who are those five?

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:55.500
There are lots of possibilities, including
Bernard, Stubbs, a resurrected Teddy, or possibly

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:56.500
some new characters.

00:10:56.500 --> 00:11:00.130
The trailer also teases a surprising team-up
between Dolores and William.

00:11:00.130 --> 00:11:02.210
"I'm gonna save the f------ world."

00:11:02.210 --> 00:11:06.340
Opposing them is none other than Maeve, who
is very much alive, despite meeting a bloody

00:11:06.340 --> 00:11:07.840
end at the end of season 2.

00:11:08.020 --> 00:11:12.279
The action-packed trailer builds to a climactic
shot of Maeve and Dolores, both clad all in

00:11:12.280 --> 00:11:14.880
black, confronting each other on a city overpass.

00:11:15.080 --> 00:11:18.960
We may not know a lot about what to expect
from season 3, but we have no doubt that the

00:11:18.960 --> 00:11:22.760
next showdown between Dolores and Maeve is
going to be one for the ages.

00:11:23.060 --> 00:11:25.220
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:11:25.220 --> 00:11:28.480
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
stuff are coming soon.

